# WatchPlay — git attributes.
#
# The protocol traces and the Gradle wrapper JAR are committed binaries. Without
# these declarations git may treat them as text and rewrite line endings on
# checkout, which corrupts the byte-for-byte agreement between
# docs/spec/02-wire-format.md and the committed traces. CI verifies that
# agreement, so a silent normalisation would show up as a puzzling red build on
# a machine whose core.autocrlf differs from yours.

# Committed protocol traces: the ground truth for parser conformance tests.
*.bin binary
examples/protocol-traces/*.bin -text -diff

# Gradle wrapper must stay byte-identical to the upstream distribution.
*.jar binary

# Keep spec source files as LF everywhere so the quoted hex dumps and tables
# diff cleanly across platforms.
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.kt text eol=lf
*.kts text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf

# Document figures: the .mmd sources and the SVGs rendered from them. Keep both
# as LF so a Windows checkout does not rewrite the committed SVG.
*.mmd text eol=lf
*.svg text eol=lf

# Windows-only launcher scripts keep CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
gradlew text eol=lf
